-- Phase 2a of the NPC / bestiary work: the 29 named people the imported books stat
-- who are not gods - the first rows of notable_npcs (migration 072) and their
-- 69 attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-notable-npcs.sql
--
-- FOUND by listing every stat block carrying a Real/True/Greek Name line or a
-- numeric experience level (the filing rule of migration 072) in the cached
-- books, minus the gods, which are Phase 2b. Underseas' Kraken is an Alien
-- Intelligence and waits for 2b with them.
--
-- EXTRACTED by one book-extract-worker per book, every number read off a 200 dpi
-- render rather than the OCR cache - the text layers carry the digit cipher -
-- and every printed folio checked against scripts/books.json. RECONCILED by
-- book-reconcile against the renders, row by row; its corrections are applied.
--
-- WHAT A ROW HOLDS. The book's numbers for one person, as printed: combat totals
-- already include every bonus, which is why a campaign copy applies no class
-- rules over them. `skills` holds percentile skills only; W.P.s and Hand to Hand
-- are in skills_note. Magic, psionics and super powers are the book's NAMES,
-- prose by decision (2026-09-17). description, disposition and
-- natural_abilities are short paraphrases - no sentence is the book's.
--
-- BY BOOK:
--   Rifts World Book 16: Federation of Magic (9): Brethan D'zir, Coran D'zir, Leizak D'zir, Alistair Dunscon, Mestoph Denali, Kara Zayne, Dan Ironforge, K'zaa, Dragonbane
--   Revised Heroes Unlimited (5): Power Master, Task Master, Shadow Master, Brain Storm, Gold Falcon
--   Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec (6): James Lome, Sylvain Richard, Julie Tremblay, Jean Desjardins, Robert Miller, Robert Carlye
--   Rifts World Book 14: New West (6): Gwen Severson, Jacob Whispering Wind, Essai Ramirez, Katherine Delgado, Thadius Geller, Roderick Warrington III
--   Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising (2): Arthur Night, Knight Hunter
--   Rifts Dimension Book 2: Phase World (1): Knife Master

  'brethan-dzir', 'Brethan D''zir', NULL, 'High Lord Magus, First Among Equals', 'rifts', 'Unknown; supernatural on a god-like level', '24th level Lord Magus', 24, 'Scrupulous', 'Thousands if not millions of years old', '17 feet (5.2 m) tall', 'two tons', '{"IQ":24,"ME":22,"MA":26,"PS":42,"PP":24,"PE":30,"PB":14,"Spd":25}', NULL, NULL, 16500, 8000, NULL, NULL, 15, '{"attacks":9,"initiative":6,"strike":9,"parry":9,"dodge":9,"pull":6,"roll":4}', 'critical hit natural 19-20; Knockout on natural 20; 9 physical or 3 spell attacks/melee; teleport self 98%, dimensional teleport 90%', '[{"name":"Communication skills (all)","pct":98},{"name":"Medical skills (all)","pct":98},{"name":"Science skills (all)","pct":98},{"name":"Technical skills (all)","pct":86},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Climbing (dual roll 90%/80%)","pct":90},{"name":"Language: American","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Spanish","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Elven/Dragonese","pct":98},{"name":"Language: Demongogian","pct":98}]', 'Hunting (no % printed); W.P. sword, W.P. staff, W.P. blunt; literate in all languages he speaks at 98%', 'Feeds on ley line magic, no need to eat/drink; fast bio-regen; invisibility at will; keen hawk-like sight; immune to S.D.C. weapons; resists heat/cold; teleports.', 'All common spell magic in Rifts RPG and this book, levels 1-15; Good knowledge of dimensional travel; Spell Strength 17', NULL, 'Epic Scale (optional); God-like perceptions (optional); Deific Power: Create Deific Portal; Deific Power: Display Deific Omen; Deific Power: Manifestation', NULL, 'Access to rare Techno-Wizard and magical devices (will not use rune weapons, Bio-Wizard creations, or anything linked to Necromancy/Undead)', NULL, 'Calm, dignified and diplomatic leader; slow to anger but capable of great force when needed.', 'His brothers (Coran, Leizak); Residents of Dweomer City; Federation of Magic factions loyal to him', 'Grim Reapers; Lord Alistair Dunscon; Coalition States; the Undead; Necromancers; Witches', 'Eldest and public spokesman of The Three, the godlike Lords of Magic who rule Dweomer City; head of the Brotherhood of Magic.', 'Rifts World Book 16: Federation of Magic p.25');
